1
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,256
<i>Finally!</i>

2
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:09,383
<i>I've been looking
for you everywhere.</i>

3
00:00:09,384 --> 00:00:11,636
I know where the White Lotus
are being held.

4
00:00:11,637 --> 00:00:14,222
I will always be team Avatar.

5
00:00:14,223 --> 00:00:16,766
<i>We've located
your Avatar.</i>

6
00:00:16,767 --> 00:00:19,018
<i>With our newfound knowledge
of the spirit energy,</i>

7
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:23,023
<i>we can strike two rattle-ravens
with one arrow.</i>

8
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:26,902
<i>I'll use the Avatar's own
weapon against her!</i>

9
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:29,446
Get to high ground!

10
00:00:30,781 --> 00:00:32,280
It's an ambush!

11
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:34,743
I was able to capture

12
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:36,036
the Faceless Queen.

13
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:39,373
<i>I had a hunch the Avatar
was hiding in the ruins.</i>

14
00:00:39,498 --> 00:00:41,208
<i>I wasn't able to find her.</i>

15
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:43,751
<i>The Avatar
has retaliated.</i>

16
00:01:00,477 --> 00:01:03,313
Ha! I can't believe
you fell for that!

17
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:06,108
You cheated, Karthik!

18
00:01:06,233 --> 00:01:09,360
Enemies don't bring sparring
dummies to the battlefield.

19
00:01:09,361 --> 00:01:11,028
I told you, Kayoko,

20
00:01:11,029 --> 00:01:13,490
the Brigade needs
to be ready for anything.

21
00:01:15,534 --> 00:01:17,910
Remind me, why does
the council's apprentice

22
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:19,078
want basic training?

23
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,830
If I'm going to be
on the council,

24
00:01:20,831 --> 00:01:22,331
I need to know
how to protect it.

25
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:23,541
That's my job.

26
00:01:23,542 --> 00:01:24,959
Yours is to keep Ellora running

27
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:25,835
from a distance.

28
00:01:25,836 --> 00:01:26,877
I'm not going to be

29
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:28,422
one of those
stuffy council members

30
00:01:28,547 --> 00:01:29,506
cut off from their haven.

31
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:32,592
I want to get my hands...

32
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:35,095
...dirty!

33
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:38,014
Not bad, not bad. But, uh...

34
00:01:38,015 --> 00:01:39,765
...not good enough!

35
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:42,560
Wait. How'd you...

36
00:01:42,561 --> 00:01:44,646
I was just holding...

37
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:47,149
That move's
called The Bandit's Slip.

38
00:01:47,274 --> 00:01:49,985
It's a little bit advanced
for someone who deals

39
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:52,570
with district planning.

40
00:01:52,571 --> 00:01:55,782
We'll see about that.

41
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:00,787
You will not take my home
from me.

42
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:06,167
<i>Fire.</i>

43
00:02:06,168 --> 00:02:07,336
<i>Air.</i>

44
00:02:07,461 --> 00:02:08,502
<i>Water.</i>

45
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:11,340
<i>Earth.</i>

46
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:15,843
<i>Long ago, the Avatar,
master of all four elements,</i>

47
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:17,929
<i>brought forth the Cataclysm.</i>

48
00:02:18,055 --> 00:02:21,140
<i>Out of the devastation,
the world built</i>

49
00:02:21,141 --> 00:02:22,517
<i>The Seven Havens.</i>

50
00:02:22,643 --> 00:02:26,354
<i>Now the Avatar has returned,
but for the first time,</i>

51
00:02:26,355 --> 00:02:28,314
<i>there are two.</i>

52
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:30,816
<i>Most fear they'll destroy
the world again,</i>

53
00:02:30,817 --> 00:02:33,779
<i>but I believe
they will save it.</i>

54
00:02:52,047 --> 00:02:55,341
I feel like I've been through
a rock tumbler.

55
00:02:55,342 --> 00:02:56,551
What...

56
00:02:56,677 --> 00:02:58,011
What happened?

57
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:02,890
We were fighting the Anomaly,
then we got pulled

58
00:03:02,891 --> 00:03:06,895
into a memory with Mom and Dad.

59
00:03:07,354 --> 00:03:10,941
You dragged us out,
like you were afraid.

60
00:03:12,359 --> 00:03:13,610
Like you knew...

61
00:03:14,194 --> 00:03:17,197
Nisha, have you seen
that memory?

62
00:03:19,074 --> 00:03:21,951
When I was alone
in the Harshlands,

63
00:03:21,952 --> 00:03:24,161
I found an Anomaly crystal.

64
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:26,665
And I saw...

65
00:03:27,165 --> 00:03:31,670
something I never, ever
want to see again.

66
00:03:32,129 --> 00:03:36,049
I'd do anything to keep you
from seeing it too.

67
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:39,135
But it's our parents.

68
00:03:39,136 --> 00:03:40,804
<i>Shelter in your homes!</i>

69
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:44,140
<i>We will outlast this threat,</i>

70
00:03:44,141 --> 00:03:46,684
<i>like we've outlasted
all threats!</i>

71
00:03:46,685 --> 00:03:48,936
<i>I repeat!</i>

72
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:50,856
<i>Take shelter in your homes!</i>

73
00:03:51,982 --> 00:03:53,942
<i>We will outlast this threat,</i>

74
00:03:54,651 --> 00:03:56,862
<i>like we've outlasted
all threats!</i>

75
00:03:57,654 --> 00:04:00,699
<i>For the survival of Ellora!</i>

76
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:03,993
But we can't just hide
from that scary bubble!

77
00:04:03,994 --> 00:04:05,828
We have to get people
outta here!

78
00:04:05,829 --> 00:04:07,706
How? No one's gonna listen

79
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:10,333
to the Big Scary Avatar
and her sister.

80
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:13,253
Follow me!

81
00:04:16,423 --> 00:04:17,298
Ooh.

82
00:04:20,719 --> 00:04:21,720
Uh...

83
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:24,263
Hey!

84
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:25,515
Um...

85
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:28,058
Eh. Just gimme a sec.
Hmm.

86
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:30,896
Yeah!

87
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:33,607
Hmm. Ah!

88
00:04:34,441 --> 00:04:37,194
Perfect! You look nothing
like yourself!

89
00:04:37,319 --> 00:04:39,112
Is it in my hair?

90
00:04:43,325 --> 00:04:44,910
Why do you get to wear <i>that</i>

91
00:04:45,035 --> 00:04:47,119
and I'm the one
with mud on my face?!

92
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,371
Come on!

93
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:51,665
How are you?

94
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:53,835
Since the Faceless raid, I mean.

95
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:55,294
I don't know.

96
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:56,546
Is everything we do really

97
00:04:56,671 --> 00:04:58,131
for the survival of Ellora?

98
00:04:58,256 --> 00:04:59,257
Of-of course!

99
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:01,133
The Chancellor is just trying

100
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:02,802
to protect us.

101
00:05:02,803 --> 00:05:05,472
Bravery, loyalty, honesty,

102
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:06,556
compassion.

103
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:09,392
That's what the Brigade
is meant to stand for.

104
00:05:09,518 --> 00:05:11,937
But now, we're just
scary bullies.

105
00:05:12,062 --> 00:05:13,897
That's the last thing
I want to be.

106
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:22,447
You go ahead,
I'll check it out.

107
00:05:29,746 --> 00:05:31,081
Shhh.

108
00:05:31,206 --> 00:05:34,458
Any chance you'd be interested
in breaking a few rules?

109
00:05:34,459 --> 00:05:35,417
Fair warning:

110
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:37,879
we could get into a <i>lot</i>
of trouble.

111
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:41,675
Since when did Mr. Squeaky Clean
become a rebel?

112
00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:44,970
Since Ellora started
being led by fear,

113
00:05:45,095 --> 00:05:47,138
instead of our ideals.

114
00:05:49,224 --> 00:05:51,434
Ready for orders,
Captain Squeaky.

115
00:06:01,570 --> 00:06:02,445
Mister!

116
00:06:02,571 --> 00:06:03,654
You need to get your family

117
00:06:03,655 --> 00:06:04,489
out of Ellora!

118
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:05,740
You can't just hide!

119
00:06:05,866 --> 00:06:06,782
Are you nuts?!

120
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:08,118
The Chancellor explicitly said

121
00:06:08,243 --> 00:06:10,787
we'll survive
only if we stay in our homes!

122
00:06:10,912 --> 00:06:12,079
Get out of the way!

123
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:12,955
- I need to get my--
- Wait!

124
00:06:12,956 --> 00:06:14,248
You need to leave Ellora!

125
00:06:14,249 --> 00:06:16,458
- It's not safe!
- What are you talking about?!

126
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:18,336
I'm not listening to <i>you,</i>
old man!

127
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:21,590
"Old man"?

128
00:06:23,341 --> 00:06:25,844
You definitely made
my eyebrows too big.

129
00:06:25,969 --> 00:06:27,052
What do we do?

130
00:06:27,053 --> 00:06:28,637
No one's listening to us.

131
00:06:38,315 --> 00:06:39,900
You thinking what I'm thinking?

132
00:06:40,025 --> 00:06:42,318
Yeah. We're the only ones
who've been able

133
00:06:42,319 --> 00:06:44,069
to tackle those Anomalies.

134
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,238
So...

135
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:47,032
it's up to us.

136
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:03,505
Whoa!

137
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:05,383
Hey, Faceless friends!
We've already tried

138
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:07,343
climbing out a bunch of--

139
00:07:07,344 --> 00:07:09,011
I like watching them struggle.

140
00:07:09,012 --> 00:07:11,181
Keep it up, bandits! Good job!

141
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:19,773
Why don't you come down here for
a proper fight, you cowards!

142
00:07:27,072 --> 00:07:29,073
I'm sorry Kayoko took

143
00:07:29,074 --> 00:07:31,283
such drastic action
with The Faceless.

144
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:32,577
How touching.

145
00:07:32,702 --> 00:07:34,995
He's a Commander and a buddy!

146
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:37,206
I don't agree with your choices,

147
00:07:37,207 --> 00:07:39,708
but I do agree
Kayoko has gone too far.

148
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:41,211
How could Ellora get this bad?

149
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:44,380
Whatever you think of me
and the Brigade, Uki,

150
00:07:44,381 --> 00:07:46,757
the people of this Haven
are innocent.

151
00:07:46,758 --> 00:07:49,009
We need to get out of here
and help them.

152
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:51,679
We don't owe
these fools anything.

153
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:53,556
Should I be insulted by that?

154
00:07:53,682 --> 00:07:55,350
Please stop talking to me.

155
00:08:00,230 --> 00:08:01,939
Do you mind?

156
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:05,151
This is no time for sleep,
your majesty.

157
00:08:07,946 --> 00:08:11,116
You'll be sorry you didn't
get your beauty rest.

158
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:18,789
What's happening?

159
00:08:18,790 --> 00:08:20,291
It's showtime.

160
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:32,803
Your boy Jae is pretty
impressive, Karthik.

161
00:08:32,804 --> 00:08:34,139
Jae?!

162
00:08:47,569 --> 00:08:49,362
This is one
of the best jailbreaks

163
00:08:49,487 --> 00:08:50,447
I've been in!

164
00:08:51,823 --> 00:08:53,824
Aw, you saved us, Lan!

165
00:08:53,825 --> 00:08:55,743
Sorry it took me so long.

166
00:08:55,744 --> 00:08:58,203
You might've been right
about Ellora

167
00:08:58,204 --> 00:09:00,372
losing some of its charm.

168
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:02,042
Oh, Lan, I've missed you.

169
00:09:03,043 --> 00:09:04,460
I could use a little help!

170
00:09:29,944 --> 00:09:31,236
Look out!

171
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:32,071
Thanks, Commander!

172
00:09:32,072 --> 00:09:33,822
Jae, remember when I said

173
00:09:33,823 --> 00:09:36,117
you'd need to make
difficult decisions one day?

174
00:09:36,743 --> 00:09:37,702
Yeah?

175
00:09:38,203 --> 00:09:39,412
You made the right one.

176
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:42,664
I knew you didn't
turn on us, Jae!

177
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:44,167
Never would, buddy!

178
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:47,419
Stop him
before he alerts the others!

179
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:54,802
Okay.

180
00:09:54,803 --> 00:09:57,430
This just got
a lot more complicated.

181
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:19,285
Whoa!

182
00:10:22,956 --> 00:10:25,250
So what now?

183
00:10:25,375 --> 00:10:27,167
We've got to stop it
from advancing,

184
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:29,462
otherwise Ellora is toast!

185
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:31,714
The Dome's kinda like
the granddaddy

186
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,550
of the Anomalies, right?

187
00:10:33,675 --> 00:10:37,302
Could we fight it back
the same way, with energy?

188
00:10:38,847 --> 00:10:40,014
If we connect with it,

189
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,641
we'll be sucked back
into that memory.

190
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:43,517
That's okay.

191
00:10:43,518 --> 00:10:45,103
As long as we're together,

192
00:10:45,228 --> 00:10:47,063
we can handle it!

193
00:10:47,522 --> 00:10:48,772
And...

194
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:50,107
maybe we can finally find out

195
00:10:50,108 --> 00:10:51,860
what happened to Mom and Dad.

196
00:10:53,111 --> 00:10:54,778
Pavi, let me do it.

197
00:10:54,779 --> 00:10:57,740
I don't want you to be haunted
by what I know.

198
00:10:58,283 --> 00:11:00,410
What did you see?! Just tell me!

199
00:11:00,535 --> 00:11:01,327
I can take it!

200
00:11:01,452 --> 00:11:04,079
Please, I need you to trust me.

201
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:06,291
I'm doing this
for the both of us.

202
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:08,208
Twin promise.

203
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:15,216
Twin promise.

204
00:11:17,302 --> 00:11:18,553
Step back.

205
00:11:54,839 --> 00:11:56,382
No! Nisha!

206
00:11:56,507 --> 00:11:57,674
Stop! Wait!

207
00:12:06,351 --> 00:12:07,477
It stopped.

208
00:12:07,602 --> 00:12:08,853
It's working!

209
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,358
We could try an earth blockade,

210
00:12:14,359 --> 00:12:16,151
uh, maybe that'll slow it down.

211
00:12:16,152 --> 00:12:17,695
We don't have enough
earthbenders.

212
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:21,114
Perhaps a lightning strike
from our firebending forces?

213
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:22,951
No, what good
would that do?

214
00:12:24,494 --> 00:12:25,495
Chancellor!

215
00:12:25,954 --> 00:12:27,455
We may have a problem.

216
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:34,379
I knew it!

217
00:12:34,504 --> 00:12:36,964
Datu! The prisoners!
They've escaped!

218
00:12:36,965 --> 00:12:39,300
They're being lead by
a rogue airbender.

219
00:12:39,801 --> 00:12:40,843
Jae!

220
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:42,971
Go! Deal with the prisoners!

221
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:44,889
Fellow Ellorans!

222
00:12:45,390 --> 00:12:48,935
<i>The Avatar has wormed her way
back into the haven!</i>

223
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:50,644
<i>She is on the west wall,</i>

224
00:12:50,645 --> 00:12:53,773
<i>pulling the dangerous
energy sphere towards us!</i>

225
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:56,984
<i>I beg you,
help keep our home safe!</i>

226
00:12:56,985 --> 00:12:58,945
She's a danger
to everyone!

227
00:12:59,070 --> 00:13:01,238
- We can't have another Avatar!
- She's a danger to everyone!

228
00:13:01,239 --> 00:13:04,492
Get the Avatar!
Before it's too late!

229
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:12,834
I'm sorry!

230
00:13:12,959 --> 00:13:14,002
We're trying to help!

231
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:28,516
The exit through the hospital
is just up ahead!

232
00:13:30,685 --> 00:13:31,935
Datu?!

233
00:13:31,936 --> 00:13:34,272
I wanted so badly
to believe you'd changed.

234
00:13:34,772 --> 00:13:37,483
But I don't even know
who you are anymore, Jae.

235
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:41,737
I hated lying to you, Datu,
but I have changed.

236
00:13:41,738 --> 00:13:44,032
I won't just swallow what's told
to me anymore.

237
00:13:44,157 --> 00:13:47,034
What you and Kayoko
are doing is wrong.

238
00:13:47,035 --> 00:13:48,202
So...

239
00:13:48,328 --> 00:13:50,371
I guess our relationship
is over.

240
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:54,541
Did you just figure that out??

241
00:13:54,542 --> 00:13:58,045
You're all under arrest,
by order of the Chancellor!

242
00:14:01,883 --> 00:14:05,678
Surrender now and perhaps
she'll consider leniency.

243
00:14:06,262 --> 00:14:09,306
The only thing your Chancellor
will consider

244
00:14:09,307 --> 00:14:11,809
is a swift punishment
or a slow one.

245
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:14,896
I guess you'll find out
soon enough. Get them!

246
00:14:25,073 --> 00:14:26,366
Get him!

247
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:48,136
Not bad for a new recruit.

248
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:51,307
Go! Now.
They won't be held for long.

249
00:14:51,432 --> 00:14:52,517
Jae, come on!

250
00:14:52,642 --> 00:14:55,602
Go! I'll catch up with you.

251
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:04,861
I guess I can
finally tell you...

252
00:15:04,862 --> 00:15:06,864
I've always hated your cooking!

253
00:15:08,199 --> 00:15:10,617
Okay. Now that's just hurtful!

254
00:15:20,962 --> 00:15:22,587
I still care about you, Jae.

255
00:15:22,588 --> 00:15:23,923
Don't do anything stupid.

256
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:26,425
Oh, it's <i>way</i> too late for that.

257
00:15:44,444 --> 00:15:47,028
- Stop her!
- She's a danger to everyone!

258
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:49,282
- We must destroy her!
- Before it's too late!

259
00:15:50,533 --> 00:15:51,617
Sorry about this!

260
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:55,746
It'd probably be better for
everyone if you just go home!

261
00:15:57,915 --> 00:16:00,750
Maybe relax
with some tea!

262
00:16:03,463 --> 00:16:05,256
Pavi! Stop being so nice

263
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:07,841
and take care
of this raging mob!

264
00:16:11,471 --> 00:16:14,514
I don't know how much longer
I can hold everyone off!

265
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:16,016
Can't...

266
00:16:16,017 --> 00:16:17,435
let go!

267
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:20,980
You gotta keep 'em back!

268
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:26,277
Quick, to the wall!

269
00:16:26,402 --> 00:16:28,279
The Avatar is back!

270
00:16:28,404 --> 00:16:30,114
We must stop her!

271
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:32,032
After them!

272
00:16:32,033 --> 00:16:33,826
We need to find the girls!

273
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:37,580
Look, I know we're
on opposing sides,

274
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:40,458
but the Avatar isn't just meant
to protect Ellora.

275
00:16:40,583 --> 00:16:42,417
She's here
to save the whole world,

276
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:44,462
and right now,
she needs our help.

277
00:16:44,587 --> 00:16:45,922
Will you join us?

278
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:50,510
I suppose I could help
those silly kids out.

279
00:16:51,135 --> 00:16:52,552
My queen!

280
00:16:52,553 --> 00:16:54,180
You know my rule.

281
00:16:54,305 --> 00:16:56,848
We all decide
our own paths in life.

282
00:16:56,849 --> 00:17:00,143
Freedom of choice
is all I've ever wanted.

283
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:03,189
I choose to help
the Avatar and my home.

284
00:17:03,314 --> 00:17:05,358
I can't thank you both enough.

285
00:17:09,444 --> 00:17:11,030
I don't like this.

286
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:12,656
I'm not asking you to.

287
00:17:27,505 --> 00:17:29,090
Shield your faces!

288
00:17:49,694 --> 00:17:51,279
Pavi! Are you okay?!

289
00:17:51,404 --> 00:17:54,115
Can I take a nap now?

290
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:04,124
I'm not sure
how much longer...

291
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:08,629
<i>Don't let go!
Why did you leave me?!</i>

292
00:18:11,048 --> 00:18:12,883
Nisha, listen to me.

293
00:18:14,051 --> 00:18:15,760
Commander?

294
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:18,139
You were born for this.

295
00:18:18,264 --> 00:18:21,308
You have all the strength
you need inside of you.

296
00:18:24,729 --> 00:18:27,939
I can do this. I can do this.

297
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:36,866
Uh, Commander?

298
00:18:36,991 --> 00:18:38,284
Danger ahead!

299
00:18:41,495 --> 00:18:43,288
Go! Stop them!

300
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:12,443
Stop! We'll stand down!

301
00:19:12,568 --> 00:19:14,986
I just want to talk to you,
Kayoko.

302
00:19:19,033 --> 00:19:21,494
I suppose
I should be impressed.

303
00:19:22,078 --> 00:19:25,414
You've added jailbreaking
to your list of dubious talents.

304
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:28,166
Kayoko, you have no reason
to trust me.

305
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:31,712
I-I hate that I took advantage
of our relationship.

306
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:35,006
Especially since you still
mean the world to me.

307
00:19:35,007 --> 00:19:36,342
Karthik, stop.

308
00:19:36,759 --> 00:19:38,552
Why rub salt in that wound?

309
00:19:38,678 --> 00:19:40,553
Kayoko, I swear to you,

310
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:43,431
the Avatar isn't trying
to destroy our home.

311
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:45,726
She is the key to saving it.

312
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:48,229
No bender can stop
this dangerous energy

313
00:19:48,354 --> 00:19:50,189
other than her.

314
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:52,566
Kayoko, let me fix what I broke.

315
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:56,403
Let's both help her
and save Ellora.

316
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:02,201
Like old times?

317
00:20:11,085 --> 00:20:12,962
Kayoko!

318
00:20:38,696 --> 00:20:40,614
Why is it still coming?

319
00:20:57,006 --> 00:20:57,964
No!

320
00:20:57,965 --> 00:20:58,966
No!

321
00:21:05,014 --> 00:21:06,807
Pavi! Nisha!

322
00:21:06,932 --> 00:21:09,268
Fall back! Fall back!

323
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:11,352
Save as many as you can!

324
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:14,315
Get everyone out of Ellora!

325
00:21:18,319 --> 00:21:20,320
- No!
- Pavi!

326
00:21:20,321 --> 00:21:21,947
Nisha!

327
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:36,419
What happened?

328
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:39,048
This doesn't look like Ellora.

329
00:21:41,175 --> 00:21:42,635
Hello?

330
00:21:43,427 --> 00:21:46,806
So, how do we get out of here?

331
00:21:46,931 --> 00:21:48,556
Finally! I found you.

332
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:56,941
Mom?!

